# ISSUES — {{PROJECT}}

Noticed, not acted on. One entry per observation; update status inline; work
the backlog via `/issues`. Open entries use the `- [ ]` checkbox form —
session_boot counts them at every session start.

<!-- Entry format (newest first; patterns quoted mid-line so session_boot's
open-entry counter never counts these examples as real open issues):
Open entry: "- [ ] YYYY-MM-DD — the observation, concrete enough to
            investigate cold — suggested action + one-line effort/risk guess."
Closed:     "- [x] RESOLVED (YYYY-MM-DD) — outcome" — keep the closed line
            when the history is instructive; delete it when it isn't.

Rules:
- An issue entry is an observation, not a commitment — never act on one
  unasked; /issues is the interactive way to work them.
- If investigation shows the observation was stale or wrong, close it with a
  note saying why — that's a finding too.
-->
